20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=20</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 74.37)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="1.0pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.69,0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 11.81 0 L 23.62 0"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#0000CC;" fill="#0000CC"><path style="fill:none" d="M 11.81 0 C 11.81 0 11.81 0 11.81 0 C 11.81 0 11.81 0 11.81 0 C 11.81 0 11.81 0 11.81 0 C 11.81 0 11.81 0 11.81 0 Z M 11.81 0"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 28.47 0) translate(21.94,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.17 -3.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="38.34"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F6.pic4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=50</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 90.9)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke-width="1.0pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.69,0)"><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 11.81 0 L 23.62 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CC0000;" fill="#CC0000" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 11.81 0 C 11.81 0 11.81 0 11.81 0 C 11.81 0 11.81 0 11.81 0 C 11.81 0 11.81 0 11.81 0 C 11.81 0 11.81 0 11.81 0 Z M 11.81 0"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 25.01 0) translate(25.39,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -22.63 -3.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.27em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="45.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F6.pic4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=200</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>The impact of the <math id="A3.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> value on performance on different datasets. From left to right and top to bottom: CIFAR-10, CIFAR-100, Fashion-MNIST, EMNIST-Letters. The plots show the validation accuracy for different <math id="A3.F6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Even though the same model is used, there is great difference between optimal <math id="A3.F6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in Section <a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4 Effect of 𝜏 on MNIST Datasets ‣ 5 Results ‣ From MNIST to ImageNet: Understanding the Scalability Boundaries of Differentiable Logic Gate Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>, per-class accuracy differs greatly for different <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. We analyze this for MNIST. The accuracies are shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix C Impact of 𝜏 ‣ From MNIST to ImageNet: Understanding the Scalability Boundaries of Differentiable Logic Gate Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. Easily classifiable digits like 1 and 0 show good performance for all <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. However, performance varies a lot more for small <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as opposed to large <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
